# Try the API by hand (Rider, or VS Code with the REST Client extension).
# 1. Run the identity server and the API (docs/local-development.md, step 7).
# 2. Get an access token from the identity server's .http file, using a client that asks for
#    bjk.media bjk.profiles bjk.posts, and paste it below.

@api = https://localhost:5101
@token = <paste an access token>

### Health
GET {{api}}/health

### The public feed (no token needed)
GET {{api}}/api/posts

### Create my profile
POST {{api}}/api/profiles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "roadhog", "displayName": "Road Hog", "location": "Leeds" }

### My profile
GET {{api}}/api/profiles/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ask for an upload link, then PUT the file to upload.url with the Content-Type it gives you
POST {{api}}/api/media/uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fileName": "dashcam.mp4", "contentType": "video/mp4", "sizeBytes": 1048576 }

### After uploading: queue it for processing
@mediaId = <mediaId from above>
POST {{api}}/api/media/{{mediaId}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My uploads
GET {{api}}/api/media/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Post an incident (the media must be Ready; needs a confirmed email)
POST {{api}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Undertaking on the M62",
  "description": "Lorry undertakes at junction 26.",
  "category": "DangerousOvertaking",
  "incidentAt": "2026-10-18T08:30:00Z",
  "latitude": 53.7457,
  "longitude": -1.7181,
  "placeName": "M62 J26",
  "mediaIds": [ "{{mediaId}}" ]
}

### Download my data
GET {{api}}/api/me/data-export
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
